    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0396" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg348"/>

                <head>Mr. Johnson to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 29, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to forward herewith three
                    copies of the recent correspondence between the United States and Great Britain
                    on the question of a treaty on the subject of naturalization, and likewise
                    respecting the imprisonment of Messrs. Warren and Costello, which have just been
                    issued for the use of Parliament.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>REVERDY JOHNSON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




